aft":true,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/118635","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118635","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118635.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118635.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Note: This PR is created entirely as proof of concept and feature proposal to evaluate the idea.\r\n\r\nAdds floating \"game view\" toolbar to the non-embedded running project, and intended to replace floating embedded mode (at least as a default option).\r\n\r\n- Unlike limited (no full-screen, most window/screen related methods do nothing, no multiple native windows on macOS) floating embedded mode, project runs as it would after export, and more useful for testing.\r\n- Floating toolbar should be usable in (non-exclusive) full-screen mode as well.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4240c438-c24b-411c-bb28-58fdfcdf2297\r\n\r\n### Known issues:\r\n- Toolbar is part of the running projects and do not follow editor theme.\r\n- Toolbar is moving with the main project window on macOS, but not on Windows/X11/Wayland. This is default transient window behavior on macOS, other platforms will need some extra handling to behave the same.","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118635/reactions","total_count":10,"+1":5,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":3},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118635/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}